{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>הורד</b> Three times in the Masorah: הורד עדיך. באף עמים הורד אלהים. הורד אותם אל המים בגדעון. Because He said to him הורד עדיך, Moses was afraid of the anger and wrath, as written באף עמים הורד. And just as here there was idolatry, there too הורד אותם אל המים to separate idol worshippers, for all who kneeled on their knees to drink — a sign that they worshipped idols. And he set them apart alone."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {0 "עכו\"ם read as עבודת כוכבים ומזלות (idolatry); ע\"ג as עבודת גילולים (idol worship)."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:15:01.200938325Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}